WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.620
Sam, in the sort of limited time we have left - I know we're getting to the end here - I did want to base with you about

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:13.520
white supremacy a little bit and and manifestos, because I was- I took some criticism years ago when I said

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:22.500
an Islamic terrorist or perpetrator, who states that their motivations were related to Islam,

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.900
should be considered genuine and serious, and while there may be other aggravating factors which we can talk about,

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:35.400
that needs to be taken seriously. And I believe that. And in the same way when I hear about,

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:40.800
you know, a perpetrator that is apparently a white supremacist who

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:47.700
was participating in all of the known places on the internet, which I don't even need to name and there's no point in naming them,

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:55.700
and they say that these were motivating factors, I believe- unless I have a really specific reason to think otherwise,

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:02.580
I also believe that they're genuine. And I've seen that you've talked about the idea of those right-wing shooters

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:09.340
sometimes in your opinion writing a semi-bogus manifesto, maybe to confuse the media, maybe to get attention.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:14.280
And I definitely don't see it that way, absent some evidence that would change my mind.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.280
So I'm curious how you came to that conclusion...

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.840
You know, it was just based on hearing some evidence, or alleged evidence, in that area.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:31.200
And I'm actually- my next podcast is gonna be with Kathleen Belew who's a, you know, historian on this topic of white supremacy.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.320
So I'll sort of dive deeper into that and get a little more of an education there, but-

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:44.400
Yeah, I mean the the issue seems to be that there's this this other variant of, you know, troll culture

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:56.400
that is attracting, in many cases mentally unstable, isolated, you know, socially isolated, young men,

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:02.900
some percentage of whom are just be kind of viewing opportunities for violence as a kind of video game

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:13.960
and this gets mixed in with, you know, some level of racism, or white supremacy, or misogyny, or all of those things,

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:21.160
and it's not clear, you know- What really is the motivating factor?

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:27.400
I mean, again, in some cases violence is over-determined, right? So you have

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:36.880
someone who is is mentally ill, but is also enamored of some bad, you know, violence-producing ideas

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:45.100
and may also have a legitimate grievance in the world, right? And then that person goes into a synagogue,

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:54.500
or a mosque, or a school, and kills people. And then we're left trying to sort out, what was really the operating variables.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:03:03.240
But there're pure cases, right, of all of these things, too. Where it's just: you have psychologically normal people

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:10.120
who are motivated clearly by ideas and they state those ideas and there's no reason to doubt them.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:18.400
Right, and so there are clear cases of every type. I think it's far more common to have

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:28.000
socially marginalized, psychologically unwell people go in and shoot up schools.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:36.160
And I think it's also far more common to have people fitting that type join white supremacist organizations,

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:41.800
than it is to have those variables be the explanation for jihadism.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:53.880
The reason why I think jihadism is different than- and I did a solo podcast on this topic differentiating jihadism from white supremacy.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:04:02.360
I think it is an importantly different set of ideas, and most important, in a different context, right? It's a-

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:12.600
jihadism is an extremist set of ideas set within a mainstream religion and disentangling those ideas

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:22.360
from the mainstream religious ideas that people truly care about - that, you know, more than a billion people truly care about - is genuinely difficult, right?

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:28.000
And entails theological hair-splitting that is frankly not very convincing, right?

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:40.880
So it's a hard problem and it's for that reason attracting far more, you know, straightforwardly religious, normal people into its ranks.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:48.440
White supremacy is not quite the same, right? It's not- it doesn't have- it has links to Christianity,

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:56.400
but the links are not as direct, and they're not as not as broad, and they're not as connected to other things

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:02.400
that are good about Christianity, right? The things that people normal people really want about Christianity.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:10.200
And so I think it is filtering for, you know, unbalanced more deranged people, more marginal people,

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:18.000
people who have less opportunity and more grievances or pseudo-grievances. But then there are cases where,

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:26.920
you know, the violence is coming from, you know, just psychopathy or other psychopathology, right?

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:34.500
Where then whatever lip service may or may not be paid to ideas It really is just lip service.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:41.600
It's not really the ideas, and you don't know until you know but- Another point, as an example like...

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:53.440
I Think that the Columbine shooting is often talked about in the context of these, you know, online discussions of white supremacist violence.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:59.000
And I think Eric Harris in his journals wrote a fair amount about, you know, white supremacy.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:07.080
But- no one who's really looked at the details of the Columbine shooting thinks that this is a clear case of white supremacist violence.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:13.400
I mean these were really disturbed young men who decided to kill their classmates and,

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:19.920
you know, it's that this was not the Oklahoma City bombing which is which was clearly ideological.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:27.560
And so it's just- you just don't know until you know. And when I spoke about the El Paso shooting,

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:35.720
and even the Christ Church shooting, it just wasn't totally clear to me. What was what in terms of those manifestos?

